      "description": "Varies tie types. In measure 1, there is a cross-voice tie between beat 1 (in voice 1) and beat 2 (in voice 2). On beat 4, there is a enharmonic tie to the first note in measure 2. In measure 2, there are three “arpeggio ties” starting at the sixth, seventh, and eighth eighth note, respectively, tying to a chord on the first beat in measure 3. In measure 4, there is a laissez-vibrer tie on the eighth note.",
